    "answer": "The kidneys maintain blood pH at ~7.4 by tubular secretion of $\\text{H}^+$ ions into the filtrate and reabsorption of $\\text{HCO}_3^-$ (bicarbonate) back into the blood. During acidosis, more $\\text{H}^+$ is secreted and more $\\text{HCO}_3^-$ is retained; during alkalosis, the reverse occurs.",
